SPECIFICATION: "Fuzz" host plugin (Fuzz Face style)
====================================================
Purpose
-------
Reproduce a host-discovered audio effect plugin named "Fuzz". The host loads
the module because the class exposes get_name, get_knobs, get_switches, and
apply_effect. Processing models a Dallas-Arbiter Fuzz Face: two-stage
asymmetric clipping, pickup/volume sensitivity, Ge vs Si character, Q2 bias.

Language / libraries
--------------------
Python 3. Use numpy and scipy.signal only (plus stdlib dataclasses/typing).
Do not use a per-sample Python loop for the nonlinearity; vectorize with
numpy. Use SciPy SOS IIR filters with carried zi so block processing is
continuous.

Host plugin contract (must match)
---------------------------------
Dataclasses (same field names and defaults as below):

  @dataclass
  class KnobColorScheme:
      outline: str = "black"
      face: str = "white"
      needle: str = "black"

  @dataclass
  class Knob:
      name: str = "Generic"
      min: float = 0.0
      max: float = 1.0
      default: float = 0.5
      click_pts: List[float] = field(default_factory=lambda: [0.5])
      knob_color_scheme: KnobColorScheme = field(
          default_factory=lambda: KnobColorScheme(
              outline="black", face="white", needle="black"))

  @dataclass
  class Switch:
      name: str = "Enable"
      default: bool = True

Effect class MUST be named Fuzz.
get_name() MUST return "Fuzz" (self.name = "Fuzz").

The host writes live attributes from control names lowercased, then calls
apply_effect(audio, sample_rate). Do not pass knobs as arguments to
apply_effect. Read parameters with getattr(..., default) and clip knobs to
[0, 1].

apply_effect(audio, sample_rate):
  audio: float32 (preferred) in roughly [-1, 1], shape (n,) mono or
         (n, channels) interleaved-by-column.
  sample_rate: int Hz.
  If enable is False, return audio unchanged (same object or copy is fine).
  Otherwise return float32 array, same shape, peaks clipped to [-1.5, 1.5].
  Raise ValueError if ndim is not 1 or 2.

Controls
--------
Knobs (all min=0, max=1):

  name     default  click_pts                      face color
  Fuzz     0.85     [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]    "tomato"
  Volume   0.70     [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]    "wheat"
  Bias     0.55     [0.25, 0.5, 0.55, 0.65, 0.75]  "lightgreen"
  Input    1.0      [0.0, 0.4, 0.7, 1.0]           "gainsboro"

Every knob: outline="black", needle="black". Use CSS/Tk named colors, not hex,
so faces render light (not black).

Switches:
  Enable     default True   -> self.enable      (true bypass)
  Germanium  default True   -> self.germanium   (True=Ge, False=Si)

__init__ must also set matching live members:
  fuzz=0.85, volume=0.70, bias=0.55, input=1.0,
  enable=True, germanium=True
and empty filter state (see State).

DSP algorithm (per channel, identical)
--------------------------------------
Symbols:
  fuzz, volume, bias, input  in [0, 1]
  germanium bool
  x  = channel samples as float64

1) Guitar-volume / pickup load
     xin = x * (input ** 1.6)

2) Redesign filters if sample_rate, channel count, or germanium changed.
   First-order Butterworth SOS via scipy.signal.butter(..., output="sos"):
     nyq = 0.5 * sample_rate
     if germanium:  hp=90 Hz,  lp1=4200 Hz, lp2=2800 Hz
     else:          hp=140 Hz, lp1=7200 Hz, lp2=4500 Hz
     cap each cutoff/nyq at 0.99.
     sos_hp  = butter(1, hp/nyq,  btype="highpass", output="sos")
     sos_lp1 = butter(1, lp1/nyq, btype="lowpass",  output="sos")
     sos_lp2 = butter(1, lp2/nyq, btype="lowpass",  output="sos")
   On redesign, reset zi to zeros using sosfilt_zi(sos)[:, None] * 0
   for each channel and each of the three filters.

3) High-pass
     hp, zi_hp[ch] = sosfilt(sos_hp, xin, zi=zi_hp[ch])

4) Coefficients from knobs
     drive    = 18 + 70 * (fuzz ** 1.35)
     offset   = (0.55 - bias) * (0.35 if germanium else 0.22)
     pos_lim  = 0.55 + 0.35 * bias
     neg_lim  = 0.95 - 0.40 * bias
     softness = 0.85 if germanium else 0.38
     audio_taper(v) = (10**(v*1.5) - 1) / (10**1.5 - 1)
     out_gain = 0.15 + 1.35 * audio_taper(volume)

5) Asymmetric saturator (vectorized):
     def asym_sat(x, pos_lim, neg_lim, softness):
         xp = maximum(x, 0)
         xn = minimum(x, 0)
         yp = pos_lim * tanh(xp / (pos_lim * softness + 1e-12))
         yn = -neg_lim * tanh((-xn) / (neg_lim * softness + 1e-12))
         return yp + yn

6) Stage 1 (mild) then LP1
     st1 = asym_sat(hp * (3.2 + 4.0 * fuzz), 0.9, 0.7, softness + 0.25)
     st1, zi_lp1[ch] = sosfilt(sos_lp1, st1, zi=zi_lp1[ch])

7) Stage 2 (hard fuzz) then sag then LP2
     driven = st1 * drive + offset
     fuzzed = asym_sat(driven, pos_lim, neg_lim, softness)
     fuzzed *= 1.0 - 0.08 * tanh(abs(driven) * 0.15)
     out, zi_lp2[ch] = sosfilt(sos_lp2, fuzzed, zi=zi_lp2[ch])

8) Output
     y = clip(out * out_gain, -1.5, 1.5).astype(float32)

Stereo: process each column independently with its own zi triple.
Do not mix channels.

State to keep on the instance
-----------------------------
_sos_hp, _sos_lp1, _sos_lp2
_zi_hp, _zi_lp1, _zi_lp2   # lists length = channel count
_last_sr, _last_ch, _last_ge
Rebuild SOS + zero zi when any of sr / ch / germanium change.

Intended audible / scope behavior
---------------------------------
Germanium ON: softer tanh, rounded clip plateaus, darker (lower LPs),
stronger bias offset, less edge hash.
Germanium OFF (silicon): harder clip, flatter tops, steeper edges,
brighter spectrum.
Fuzz: gain / splat. Volume: audio-taper output. Bias: clip symmetry
(sweet spot ~0.5-0.6). Input: rolling down cleans toward crunch, not
only quieter (Fuzz Face pickup interaction).

File / discovery
----------------
Single class Fuzz in a module the host auto-imports. No extra public
API required. Optional module docstring stating the four discovery
methods.